        ui_v < 100 ? ( gfx_set(1, 1, 1, 0.9); gfx_setfont(5); sprintf(#ui_t, "%d", ui_v); xctr(ui_cx, ui_ry, ui_cwid, 16, #ui_t); );
      );
      (ui_hov && uiClick) ? ( ui_paint = 5; );
      (ui_paint == 5 && uiLmb && ui_act && mX >= ui_cx && mX < ui_cx + ui_cwid) ? (
        ui_pv = min(100, max(0, floor((ui_ry + 16 - mY) / 16 * 100 + 0.5)));
        ui_pv != ui_v ? ( pg_postU(18, ui_s, ui_pv, 0); );
      );
      (ui_hov && uiRClk) ? ( pg_postU(18, ui_s, 100, 0); );
    );
  );
  pg_hint(ui_gx, ui_ry, ui_gw, 16,
    ui_rr == 0 ? "ACCENT: step is played with ACC VEL (click / drag to paint, right-click clears). Only on normal gate steps. Key A over a step"
    : ui_rr == 1 ? "SLIDE: legato into the next step (overlapping notes). Only sounds if the next step is a normal gate step. Key S over a step"
    : ui_rr == 2 ? "GATE: click cycles OFF, ON, TIE (tie = note holds into this step, no new note). Keys G (on/off) and T (tie) over a step"
    : ui_rr == 3 ? "OCT: octave shift -1 / 0 / +1 / +2 for this step (click cycles, right-click = 0). Key O over a step"
    : "PROB: chance that the step plays, 0..100 % (drag in the column, right-click = 100). Deterministic per seed. Key P cycles 100 / 75 / 50 / 25");
);

// Auswahlband ueber Roll und Spuren
ui_sel0 >= 0 ? (
  ui_ba = max(ui_sel0, ui_pg0);
  ui_bb = min(ui_sel1, ui_pg0 + ui_cols - 1);
  ui_bb >= ui_ba ? (
    colAcid(0.11); xrect(ui_gx + (ui_ba - ui_pg0) * ui_cw, ui_gy, (ui_bb - ui_ba + 1) * ui_cw, ui_ly + 94 - ui_gy);
    colAcid(0.9);
    xrect(ui_gx + (ui_ba - ui_pg0) * ui_cw, 100, (ui_bb - ui_ba + 1) * ui_cw, 2);
    xrect(ui_gx + (ui_ba - ui_pg0) * ui_cw, ui_ly + 93, (ui_bb - ui_ba + 1) * ui_cw, 1);
  );
);

// Tastatur (Hover-Fokus): nur ohne offenes Modul-Overlay (die Module lesen gfx_getchar selbst) und nur ueber Roll / Spuren
ui_hov = (inBox(ui_gx, ui_gy, ui_gw, ui_rbot - ui_gy) || inBox(ui_gx, ui_ly, ui_gw, 94)) ? 1 : 0;
ui_ps = ui_hov ? (ui_pg0 + floor((mX - ui_gx) / ui_cw)) : 0 - 1;
ui_kbOk = (tt_pb_open == 0 && tth_open == 0 && tth_edit == 0) ? 1 : 0;
ui_kbOk ? (
  loop(8,   // Review Codex 0.7.0 (R6): jeder Code wird unmittelbar vor der Verarbeitung gelesen (der neunte ging sonst verloren)
    ui_kc = gfx_getchar();
    ui_kc > 0 ? (
      tt_testok() ? ( PG_XK[0] += 1; PG_XK[1 + (PG_XK[0] - 1) % 16] = ui_kc; );
      ui_hov ? ui_key(ui_kc);
    );
  );
);

// ===== SELECTION (links unten) =====
ui_dk ? (
  panel2(12, 422, 228, 210, "SELECTION");
  ui_hs = ui_sel0 >= 0 ? 1 : 0;
  ui_ckOk = ((ui_clipKind == 2 && PG_RCL[0] > 0) || (ui_clipKind == 1 && M_CLP[0] > 0)) ? 1 : 0;
  ui_hs ? sprintf(#ui_s, "SEL %d-%d  =  %d STEPS", ui_sel0 + 1, ui_sel1 + 1, ui_sel1 - ui_sel0 + 1) : strcpy(#ui_s, "NO SELECTION = WHOLE PATTERN");
  gfx_setfont(5); ui_hs ? colAcid(1) : colInk(0.7);
  pg_strF(22, 453, 5, #ui_s, 208, 14);
  pg_hint(18, 450, 216, 20, "Current step selection. The edit buttons act on it; without a selection they act on the whole pattern");
  ui_op(22, 474, 48, 22, "COPY", "Copy the selected steps (the whole slot without a selection)", 1) ? ( ui_aCopy(); );
  ui_op(74, 474, 48, 22, "CUT", "Cut: copy, then clear the selected steps (the whole slot without a selection)", 1) ? ( ui_aCut(); );
  ui_op(126, 474, 48, 22, "PASTE", "Paste at the start of the selection (step 1 without a selection); clipped at the pattern end. After a whole-slot COPY: replaces the slot", ui_ckOk) ? ( ui_aPaste(ui_hs ? ui_sel0 : 0); );
  ui_op(178, 474, 48, 22, "CLR", "Clear the selected steps (gate off, pitches stay as ghost notes). Without a selection: clear the whole slot", 1) ? ( ui_aClr(); );
  ui_op(22, 500, 48, 22, "<ROT", "Rotate the selection one step earlier (wraps inside the selection; the whole pattern without a selection)", 1) ? ( ui_aRot(0 - 1); );
  ui_op(74, 500, 48, 22, "ROT>", "Rotate the selection one step later (wraps inside the selection)", 1) ? ( ui_aRot(1); );
  ui_op(126, 500, 48, 22, "REV", "Reverse the selection (slides follow their link, ties stay attached to their note)", 1) ? ( ui_aRev(); );
  ui_op(178, 500, 48, 22, "INV", "Invert the pitches of the selection around ROOT, snapped to the scale", 1) ? ( ui_aInv(); );
  ui_op(22, 526, 48, 22, "ST-", "Transpose the selection one scale degree down (the whole pattern without a selection)", 1) ? ( ui_aTrans(0 - 1); );
  ui_op(74, 526, 48, 22, "ST+", "Transpose the selection one scale degree up", 1) ? ( ui_aTrans(1); );
  ui_op(126, 526, 48, 22, "OCT-", "Selection one octave down (limit -1)", 1) ? ( ui_aOct(0 - 1); );
  ui_op(178, 526, 48, 22, "OCT+", "Selection one octave up (limit +2)", 1) ? ( ui_aOct(1); );
  ui_op(22, 552, 48, 22, "DUP", "Duplicate the selection right after itself (clipped at the pattern end)", ui_hs) ? ( ui_aDup(); );
  ui_op(74, 552, 48, 22, "DBL", "Double: 16 steps become 32 (second half = copy). Only for length <= 16", ui_len <= 16) ? ( ui_send(6, 0, 0, 0); );
  ui_op(126, 552, 48, 22, "ALL", "Select all steps", 1) ? ( ui_sel0 = 0; ui_sel1 = ui_len - 1; ui_anc = 0; );
  ui_op(178, 552, 48, 22, "NONE", "Clear the selection", ui_hs) ? ( ui_sel0 = 0 - 1; ui_sel1 = 0 - 1; );
  ui_tgt == ui_slot ? ( ui_tgt = (ui_slot + 1) % 8; );
  sprintf(#cmb_txt, "TO SLOT %c", 65 + ui_tgt);
  ui_tgt = combo(34, 22, 578, 140, 22, ui_tgt, 8);
  pg_hint(22, 578, 140, 22, "Target slot for the copy to the right (click = next, arrows = -/+)");
  ui_op(168, 578, 58, 22, "COPY>", "Copy the selected steps into the target slot at the same positions (undoable; a shorter target pattern is extended)", ui_hs && ui_tgt != ui_slot) ? ( ui_send(51, ui_sel0, ui_sel1, ui_tgt); );
  // Step-Locks (0.7.0): gesperrte Steps aendern GENERATE, MUTATE und REROLL nicht (Muster-Edits von Hand bleiben moeglich)
  ui_op(22, 604, 48, 22, "LOCK", "Lock the selected steps (the whole pattern without a selection): GENERATE, MUTATE and the REROLL buttons leave them alone. Key L toggles the step under the pointer", 1) ? ( ui_aLock(1); );
  ui_op(74, 604, 48, 22, "UNLK", "Unlock the selected steps (the whole pattern without a selection)", ui_lkOn) ? ( ui_aLock(0); );
  ui_op(126, 604, 100, 22, "CLEAR LOCKS", "Unlock all steps of the active slot", ui_lkOn) ? ( ui_send(74, 0, 31, 3); );
);

// ===== DECK (rechts unten): Reiter GENERATE / OUTPUT / SONG + GENERATE / MUTATE =====
ui_dty = ui_dk ? 424 : 606;
ui_dk ? ( panelBox(248, 422, 640, 210); );
gfx_setfont(5);
ui_i = 0;
loop(5,
  ui_j = ui_i;
  ui_i += 1;
  btn(256 + ui_j * 77, ui_dty, 74, 20, ui_tab == ui_j, ui_j == 0 ? "GENERATE" : ui_j == 1 ? "OUTPUT" : ui_j == 2 ? "SONG" : ui_j == 3 ? "GALLERY" : "LIBRARY") ? ( ui_tab = ui_j; ui_deckOpen = 1; );
  pg_hint(256 + ui_j * 77, ui_dty, 74, 20, ui_j == 0 ? "Generator settings: algorithm, scale, seed, mutate"
    : ui_j == 1 ? "MIDI output settings: rate, channel, swing, velocities, humanize, FOLLOW, SEQ LINK"
    : ui_j == 2 ? "Song chain, chain editing, timeline and slot overview"
    : ui_j == 3 ? "Gallery: eight candidates from the current settings (each = GENERATE with its seed), partial reroll, seed history"
    : "Library: the 32 style patterns with a preview, click = load into the active slot");
);
btn(644, ui_dty, 108, 20, 1, "GENERATE") ? ( ui_send(1, 0, 0, 0); );
pg_hint(644, ui_dty, 108, 20, "GENERATE: new pattern in the active slot from the settings (locked steps stay). Seed locked = same pattern every time");
btn(756, ui_dty, 96, 20, 1, "MUTATE") ? ( ui_aMut(); );
pg_hint(756, ui_dty, 96, 20, "MUTATE: changes AMOUNT steps, inside the selection if there is one (else in the FROM..TO range) - note / accent / slide / gate as selected. Locked steps stay");
btn(858, ui_dty, 24, 20, 0, ui_dk ? "v" : "^") ? ( ui_deckOpen = 1 - ui_deckOpen; );
pg_hint(858, ui_dty, 24, 20, ui_dk ? "Collapse the deck: the roll gets the whole height and shows the full pitch range (FOCUS). Click a tab to open it again" : "Open the deck");

ui_dk && ui_tab == 0 ? (
  // ---- GENERATE ----
  gfx_setfont(5);
  pg_kn(1, 8, 284, 470, 14, 0, 100, 50, "DENSITY", 0, "DENSITY: share of steps that play (e.g. 50 % of 16 = 8 steps; DENS VAR spreads the count around it)", 1);
  pg_kn(2, 9, 356, 470, 14, 0, 100, 30, "ACCENT", 0, "ACCENT %: chance that a playing step is accented", 1);
  pg_kn(3, 10, 428, 470, 14, 0, 100, 20, "SLIDE", 0, "SLIDE %: share of the playing steps that slide into the next playing step (e.g. 20 % of 8 notes = 2 slides; the rhythm is built so that neighbours exist)", 1);
  pg_kn(4, 11, 500, 470, 14, 0, 100, 20, "OCT JUMP", 0, "OCT JUMP %: chance of an octave jump (+1 / +2), limited by RANGE", 1);
  pg_kn(5, 12, 572, 470, 14, 0, 100, 25, "REPEAT", 0, "REPEAT %: tendency to repeat the previous note", 1);
  pg_kn(6, 13, 644, 470, 14, 5, 24, 12, "RANGE st", 0, "RANGE: ambitus in semitones above ROOT (5..24). No note leaves 0..RANGE", 1);
  pg_kn(7, 14, 716, 470, 14, 0, 100, 20, "TENSION", 0, "TENSION %: share of dissonant tones (b2, tritone) - only if the scale contains them", 1);
  pg_kn(8, 15, 788, 470, 14, 0, 100, 40, "SYNCOPATION", 0, "SYNCOPATION %: moves the notes from the downbeats to the offbeats", 1);
  pg_kn(9, 16, 860, 470, 14, 0, 100, 10, "TIES", 0, "TIES %: chance that a step following a note becomes a tie (holds the note)", 1);
  // Algorithmus / Skala
  pg_algoStr(floor(slider4));
  pg_combo(22, 4, 256, 520, 148, 22, 6, 0);
  pg_hint(256, 520, 148, 22, "Algorithm: random walk, Markov chain, Euclid rhythm + walk, motif with variation, classic mutation of the library, or TECHNO BASS: weighted rhythm recipes and slot roles A call / B variation / C answer / D fill");
  pg_noteStr(floor(slider6));
  pg_combo(23, 6, 410, 520, 52, 22, 12, 0);
  pg_hint(410, 520, 52, 22, "Root note (C..B). The pattern lives above C2 + root");
  pg_scaleStr(floor(slider5));
  pg_combo(24, 5, 468, 520, 148, 22, 10, 0);
  pg_hint(468, 520, 148, 22, "Scale. CUSTOM uses the 12 keys to the right");
  ui_mk = pg_mask();
  ui_i = 0;
  loop(12,
    ui_j = ui_i;
    ui_i += 1;
    ui_kx = 624 + ui_j * 21;
    ui_on = floor(ui_mk / (2 ^ ui_j)) & 1;
    ui_kh = inBox(ui_kx, 520, 20, 22) ? 1 : 0;
    pg_cell(ui_kx, 520, 20, 22, ui_on ? (ui_j == 0 ? 2 : 1) : 0, ui_kh);
    gfx_setfont(5);
    ui_on ? gfx_set(0.02, 0.05, 0.02, 1) : colInk(0.6);
    xctr(ui_kx, 520, 20, 22, ui_j == 0 ? "R" : ui_j == 1 ? "b2" : ui_j == 2 ? "2" : ui_j == 3 ? "b3" : ui_j == 4 ? "3" : ui_j == 5 ? "4" : ui_j == 6 ? "b5" : ui_j == 7 ? "5" : ui_j == 8 ? "b6" : ui_j == 9 ? "6" : ui_j == 10 ? "b7" : "7");
    (ui_kh && uiClick) ? (
      ui_nm = ui_on ? ui_mk - 2 ^ ui_j : ui_mk + 2 ^ ui_j;
      pg_set(7, ui_nm);
      pg_set(5, 9);
    );
  );
  pg_hint(624, 520, 252, 22, "Scale tones above ROOT (R = root). Click a key = switch to CUSTOM and toggle that tone");
  // Seed / Lock / NEW / MUT %
  gfx_setfont(4);
  panelBox(256, 550, 90, 22);
  sprintf(#ui_s, "0x%06X", floor(slider2)); colAcid(1); xctr(256, 550, 90, 22, #ui_s);
  ui_sh = inBox(256, 550, 90, 22);
  (ui_sh && mouse_wheel != 0) ? (
    pg_set(2, min(16777215, max(0, floor(slider2) + (mouse_wheel > 0 ? 1 : 0 - 1) * ((mouse_cap & 8) ? 16 : 1))));
  );
  (ui_sh && uiRClk) ? ( pg_set(2, 0); );
  pg_hint(256, 550, 90, 22, "SEED (24 bit). Wheel = +-1 (Shift = 16), right-click = 0. With LOCK the same seed always gives the same pattern");
  // 1.0.4: Hinweis, wenn das geladene Preset von einer aelteren Generator-Generation stammt (Reserve-Wort 333)
  pg_gvNote ? (
    gfx_setfont(5); gfx_set(1, 0.55, 0, 1);
    sprintf(#ui_s, "SEED SAVED BY GEN v%d", pg_gvSt - 1); pg_strF(256, 574, 5, #ui_s, 300, 16);
    pg_hint(256, 572, 300, 14, "This preset was saved by a different generator generation; GENERATE with its stored seed may draw a different pattern. The stored patterns themselves are unaffected");
  );
  pg_tgl(3, 350, 550, 52, 22, "LOCK", "LOCK SEED: GENERATE reuses the seed (repeatable). Unlocked: every GENERATE draws a new seed");
  pg_act(406, 550, 40, 22, "NEW", "Draw a new random seed without generating") ? ( pg_postU(23, 0, 0, 0); );
  // MUT %: Slider 17 (Rate der Klassiker-Mutation), nur bei ALGO = CLASSIC MUT wirksam
  ui_mutOn = floor(slider4) == 4 ? 1 : 0;
  gfx_setfont(5); ui_mutOn ? colInk(0.85) : colInk(0.5);
  xstr(452, 556, "MUT %");
  ui_v = hsliderst(33, 486, 553, 62, 14, slider17, 0, 100, 30, 1); ui_v != slider17 ? ( pg_set(17, floor(ui_v + 0.5)); );
  sprintf(#ui_s, "%d", slider17); gfx_setfont(5); ui_mutOn ? colAcid(1) : colInk(0.5);
  xstr(554, 556, #ui_s);
  ui_mutOn == 0 ? ( gfx_set(0.02, 0.03, 0.02, 0.45); xrect(486, 553, 62, 14); );
  pg_hint(452, 550, 128, 22, "MUTATE %: per-step mutation rate of the CLASSIC MUT algorithm (a library pattern is mutated while generating). Only active with ALGO = CLASSIC MUT");
  // MUTATE WHAT
  ui_i = 0;
  loop(4,
    ui_j = ui_i;
    ui_i += 1;
    ui_bit = 2 ^ ui_j;
    ui_on = floor(slider19 / ui_bit) & 1;
    gfx_setfont(5);
    toggle(584 + ui_j * 72, 550, 68, 22, ui_on, ui_j == 0 ? "NOTE" : ui_j == 1 ? "ACC" : ui_j == 2 ? "SLIDE" : "GATE") ? (
      ui_nw = ui_on ? slider19 - ui_bit : slider19 + ui_bit;
      pg_set(19, max(1, ui_nw));
    );
    pg_hint(584 + ui_j * 72, 550, 68, 22, "Properties MUTATE may change (each mutated step gets one of the enabled ones)");
  );
  // AMOUNT / FROM / TO
  gfx_setfont(5); colInk(0.85);
  sprintf(#ui_s, "AMOUNT %d", slider18); xstr(256, 586, #ui_s);
  sprintf(#ui_s, "FROM %d", slider20); xstr(392, 586, #ui_s);
  sprintf(#ui_s, "TO %d", slider21); xstr(528, 586, #ui_s);
  ui_v = hsliderst(30, 256, 604, 120, 14, slider18, 1, 32, 4, 1); ui_v != slider18 ? ( pg_set(18, floor(ui_v + 0.5)); );
  ui_v = hsliderst(31, 392, 604, 120, 14, slider20, 1, 32, 1, 1); ui_v != slider20 ? ( pg_set(20, floor(ui_v + 0.5)); );
  ui_v = hsliderst(32, 528, 604, 120, 14, slider21, 1, 32, 32, 1); ui_v != slider21 ? ( pg_set(21, floor(ui_v + 0.5)); );
  pg_hint(256, 584, 120, 36, "AMOUNT: how many steps MUTATE changes per press");
  pg_hint(392, 584, 120, 36, "REROLL FROM: first step MUTATE may touch when nothing is selected (e.g. 9 to only vary the second half)");
  pg_hint(528, 584, 120, 36, "REROLL TO: last step MUTATE may touch when nothing is selected");
  // 0.8.0 (Stufe 5): DENS VAR (Slider 68)
  sprintf(#ui_s, "DENS VAR %d", slider68); xstr(664, 586, #ui_s);
  ui_v = hsliderst(37, 664, 604, 96, 14, slider68, 0, 100, 25, 1); ui_v != slider68 ? ( pg_set(68, floor(ui_v + 0.5)); );
  pg_hint(664, 584, 96, 36, "DENS VAR %: spreads the number of playing steps around DENSITY, symmetric, at most half the pattern length at 100 (0 = exact count). Not used by CLASSIC MUT");
  gfx_setfont(5); colInk(0.7); xstr(772, 586, "MUTATE RANGE");
  ui_hs = ui_sel0 >= 0 ? 1 : 0;
  ui_hs ? sprintf(#ui_s, "SELECTION %d-%d", ui_sel0 + 1, ui_sel1 + 1)
        : sprintf(#ui_s, "STEPS %d-%d", min(ui_len, floor(slider20)), min(ui_len, max(floor(slider20), floor(slider21))));
  ui_hs ? colAcid(1) : colInk(0.9);
  xstr(772, 604, #ui_s);
  pg_hint(772, 584, 108, 36, "Which steps MUTATE may touch right now: the selection if there is one, otherwise FROM..TO");
);

ui_dk && ui_tab == 1 ? (
  // ---- OUTPUT ----
  pg_rateStr(floor(slider22));
  pg_combo(20, 22, 256, 456, 144, 22, 4, 0);
  pg_hint(256, 456, 144, 22, "Step rate: 1/16, 1/8, 1/16 triplets, 1/32 (click = next, arrows = -/+)");
  // P25 (A5): Slider 25 ist 1..16, combo 0..15 -> Versatz 1; Anzeige geklemmt wie die Ausgabe (pg_ch = Slider - 1, 0..15)
  sprintf(#pn, "MIDI CH %d", min(16, max(1, floor(slider25))));
  pg_combo(21, 25, 408, 456, 144, 22, 16, 1);
  pg_hint(408, 456, 144, 22, "MIDI output channel. Changing it releases held notes");
  pg_tgl(29, 568, 456, 132, 22, "FOLLOW IN", "FOLLOW: incoming MIDI notes transpose the pattern (C2 = original pitch). Notes are never passed through");
  pg_tgl(34, 708, 456, 92, 22, "SEQ LINK", "SEQ LINK: publish the active pattern in gmem namespace tt303pg (sender only, see manual)");
  // 1.0.4: LINK ID (Slider 69) - welcher gmem-Block zu dieser Instanz gehoert (Mehr-Instanzen-Betrieb, siehe Manual)
  sprintf(#pn, "LINK ID %d", min(8, max(1, floor(slider69))));
  pg_combo(42, 69, 806, 456, 74, 22, 8, 1);
  pg_hint(806, 456, 74, 22, "SEQ LINK ID: which gmem block this instance publishes to (1-8, ID 1 = the original block). Give every instance read by the print actions its own ID");
  pg_kn(10, 23, 290, 516, 15, 50, 75, 50, "SWING", 0, "SWING %: delays every second step (50 = straight, 66 = triplet feel)", 1);
  pg_kn(11, 24, 370, 516, 15, 5, 100, 50, "GATE LEN", 0, "GATE LEN %: note length in steps (50 = half a step). Slide overlaps by half of it", 1);
  pg_kn(12, 26, 450, 516, 15, 1, 127, 127, "ACC VEL", 3, "ACC VEL: velocity of accented steps (TT-303 HOST mode: at or above its Accent threshold)", 1);
  pg_kn(13, 27, 530, 516, 15, 1, 127, 64, "NORM VEL", 3, "NORM VEL: velocity of normal steps (must stay below the synth's accent threshold)", 1);
  pg_kn(14, 31, 610, 516, 15, 0, 20, 0, "HUM TIME", 1, "HUMANIZE TIME ms: deterministic timing jitter +- (0 = exact grid). A step never starts before the previous one", 0.1);
  pg_kn(15, 32, 690, 516, 15, 0, 30, 0, "HUM VEL", 0, "HUMANIZE VELOCITY: deterministic velocity jitter; accents stay accents", 1);
  pg_kn(16, 28, 770, 516, 15, 1, 127, 65, "THRESH", 0, "ACC THRESHOLD of your synth (TT-303 default 65 since the Devil Fish update, 100 before): keeps humanized velocities on the right side", 1);
  pg_kn(17, 35, 850, 516, 15, -2, 2, 0, "OCTAVE", 2, "OCTAVE: transposes the output by whole octaves (C2 = pattern root at 0)", 1);
  gfx_setfont(5);
  (slider26 >= slider28 && slider27 < slider28) ? ( colAcid(0.9); pg_strF(256, 574, 5, "VELOCITIES OK FOR THRESHOLD", 300, 16); )
  : ( gfx_set(1, 0.55, 0, 1); pg_strF(256, 574, 5, "ACC VEL >= THRESH > NORM VEL !", 300, 16); );
  pg_hint(256, 572, 300, 18, "Checks that ACC VEL is at or above THRESH and NORM VEL below it, so accents stay accents on the target synth");
  // 0.8.0 (Stufe 5): SLOT QUANT / NOTE TRIG / TRIG BASE (Slider 65..67)
  pg_sqStr(floor(slider65));
  pg_combo(38, 65, 566, 568, 128, 22, 5, 0);
  pg_hint(566, 568, 128, 22, "SLOT QUANT: a slot change from the front, the keys 1..8 or NOTE TRIG waits for the next beat / bar (counted from the project start). INSTANT = immediate. Automating SLOT stays immediate; nothing waits while stopped or in SONG mode");
  pg_tgl(66, 700, 568, 92, 22, "NOTE TRIG", "NOTE TRIG: eight incoming MIDI notes from TRIG BASE switch the slots A..H (quantized like SLOT QUANT). These notes do not transpose and are not passed through");
  pg_trigStr(floor(slider67));
  pg_combo(39, 67, 798, 568, 82, 22, 4, 0);
  slider66 < 0.5 ? ( gfx_set(0.02, 0.03, 0.02, 0.45); xrect(798, 568, 82, 22); );
  pg_hint(798, 568, 82, 22, "TRIG BASE: the eight chromatic notes that switch the slots A..H (C0 = MIDI 12, C1 = 24, C3 = 48, C4 = 60). FOLLOW IN transposes with all other notes");
  colInk(0.6); pg_strF(256, 592, 5, "IN: C2 = ORIGINAL PITCH (WITH FOLLOW IN)", 300, 16);
  colInk(0.6); pg_strF(256, 610, 5, "PRINT: ACTION 'TT-303PATGEN PRINT TO MIDI ITEM' (NEEDS SEQ LINK)", 620, 16);
  pg_hint(256, 608, 620, 18, "How to turn the pattern into a MIDI item: enable SEQ LINK, select a track, run the action from the action list");
);

ui_dk && ui_tab == 2 ? (
  // ---- SONG: Kette (16 Zellen), Kettenbearbeitung, Zeitleiste, Slot-Uebersicht ----
  pg_tgl(33, 256, 456, 74, 22, "SONG", "SONG: play the chain of slots instead of the active slot");
  ui_cell = min(15, max(0, ui_cell));
  ui_i = 0;
  loop(16,
    ui_j = ui_i;
    ui_i += 1;
    ui_kx = 340 + ui_j * 34;
    ui_ky = 456;
    ui_cs = M_CHS[ui_j];
    ui_kh = inBox(ui_kx, ui_ky, 31, 22) ? 1 : 0;
    pg_cell(ui_kx, ui_ky, 31, 22, ui_cs < 0 ? 0 : (ui_j < pg_songN ? 1 : 3), ui_kh);
    ui_j == ui_cell ? ( colWhite(0.9); xrect(ui_kx + 2, ui_ky + 20, 27, 2); );
    gfx_setfont(5);
    ui_cs < 0 ? ( colInk(0.4); xctr(ui_kx, ui_ky, 31, 22, "-"); )
              : ( gfx_set(0.02, 0.05, 0.02, 1);
                  sprintf(#ui_t, M_CHR[ui_j] > 1 ? "%c%d" : "%c", 65 + ui_cs, M_CHR[ui_j]);
                  xctr(ui_kx, ui_ky, 31, 22, #ui_t); );
    ui_next = ui_cs >= 7 ? 0 - 1 : ui_cs + 1;
    (ui_kh && uiClick) ? ( ui_cell = ui_j; pg_postU(21, ui_j, ui_next, M_CHR[ui_j]); );
    (ui_kh && uiRClk) ? ( ui_cell = ui_j; pg_postU(21, ui_j, ui_cs, M_CHR[ui_j] >= 8 ? 1 : M_CHR[ui_j] + 1); );
  );
  pg_hint(340, 456, 544, 22, "Song chain (16 cells, ends at the first empty one): click = next slot / empty, right-click = repeats 1..8 (A3 = slot A three times). The underlined cell is the one the buttons below act on");
  // Kettenbearbeitung
  ui_op(256, 484, 52, 20, "INSERT", "Insert a cell with the active slot (1 repeat) after the underlined cell; the following cells move right, the last one drops out", 1) ? ( ui_send(62, min(15, ui_cell + 1), ui_slot, 1); ui_cell = min(15, ui_cell + 1); );
  ui_op(312, 484, 52, 20, "DELETE", "Delete the underlined cell; the following cells move left", 1) ? ( ui_send(63, ui_cell, 0, 0); );
  ui_op(368, 484, 34, 20, "<<", "Move the underlined cell one position to the left", ui_cell > 0) ? ( ui_send(64, ui_cell, ui_cell - 1, 0); ui_cell = ui_cell - 1; );
  ui_op(406, 484, 34, 20, ">>", "Move the underlined cell one position to the right", ui_cell < 15) ? ( ui_send(64, ui_cell, ui_cell + 1, 0); ui_cell = ui_cell + 1; );
  // Kettenlaenge: Summe Laenge x Wiederholungen bis zur ersten leeren Zelle, in Takten bei der Raster-Rate
  ui_tot = 0;
  ui_i = 0;
  loop(pg_songN,
    ui_j = ui_i;
    ui_i += 1;
    ui_tot += M_LEN[min(7, max(0, M_CHS[ui_j]))] * M_CHR[ui_j];
  );
  ui_spb = floor(slider22) == 0 ? 16 : floor(slider22) == 1 ? 8 : floor(slider22) == 2 ? 24 : 32;   // Steps je Takt (4/4)
  gfx_setfont(5); colInk(0.85);
  pg_songN > 0 ? sprintf(#ui_s, "CHAIN: %d CELL(S) = %d STEPS = %.2f BARS", pg_songN, ui_tot, ui_tot / ui_spb)
               : strcpy(#ui_s, "CHAIN: EMPTY (CLICK A CELL ABOVE)");
  xstr(452, 490, #ui_s);
  pg_hint(448, 484, 432, 20, "Length of the song chain: all cells up to the first empty one, in steps and in 4/4 bars at the current RATE");
  // Zeitleiste: ein Block je Zelle, Breite = Laenge x Wiederholungen
  panelBox(256, 510, 624, 24);
  ui_acc = 0;
  ui_i = 0;
  loop(pg_songN,
    ui_j = ui_i;
    ui_i += 1;
    ui_cs = min(7, max(0, M_CHS[ui_j]));
    ui_wd = 620 * M_LEN[ui_cs] * M_CHR[ui_j] / max(1, ui_tot);
    ui_bx = 258 + 620 * ui_acc / max(1, ui_tot);
    ui_acc += M_LEN[ui_cs] * M_CHR[ui_j];
    (ui_j & 1) ? colAcid(0.55) : colAcid(0.85);
    xrect(ui_bx, 513, max(1, ui_wd - 1), 18);
    ui_j == ui_cell ? ( colWhite(0.95); xrect(ui_bx, 530, max(1, ui_wd - 1), 2); );
    (pg_curCell === ui_j && pg_songOn) ? ( colWhite(0.22); xrect(ui_bx, 513, max(1, ui_wd - 1), 18); );   // 0.8.1: gerade spielende Zelle heller
    gfx_setfont(5); gfx_set(0.02, 0.05, 0.02, 1);
    ui_wd > 20 ? ( sprintf(#ui_t, M_CHR[ui_j] > 1 ? "%c x%d" : "%c", 65 + ui_cs, M_CHR[ui_j]); xctr(ui_bx, 513, ui_wd, 18, #ui_t); );
    (inBox(ui_bx, 513, ui_wd, 18) && uiClick) ? ( ui_cell = ui_j; );
  );
  // 0.8.1: laufender Playhead - senkrechter Strich ueber die Zeitleiste plus mitwachsende waagerechte Linie darunter (nur wenn die Kette spielt)
  (pg_songOn && pg_curCell >= 0 && pg_curTot > 0 && pg_curStep >= 0) ? (
    ui_px = 258 + 620 * pg_curQ / pg_curTot;
    ui_pw = max(2, 620 / pg_curTot);
    colWhite(0.9); xrect(258, 535, max(1, ui_px - 258 + ui_pw), 3);
    colWhite(1); xrect(ui_px, 508, ui_pw, 30);
  );
  pg_hint(256, 510, 624, 24, "Timeline of the chain: one block per cell, width = pattern length x repeats. The bright line is the playhead (it runs while the chain plays); the lit block is the cell that is playing. Click a block to underline its cell");
  // Slot-Uebersicht: acht Miniatur-Rollen, Klick waehlt den Slot
  ui_i = 0;
  loop(8,
    ui_j = ui_i;
    ui_i += 1;
    ui_bx = 256 + ui_j * 78;
    ui_by = 540;
    ui_ln = M_LEN[ui_j];
    panelBox(ui_bx, ui_by, 74, 58);
    ui_j == ui_slot ? ( colAcid(0.9); xrrect(ui_bx, ui_by, 74, 58, 3, 0); );
    (pg_sqPend && pg_sqSlot == ui_j) ? ( colWhite(floor(time_precise() * 4) & 1 ? 0.95 : 0.35); xrrect(ui_bx, ui_by, 74, 58, 3, 0); );
    ui_mini(ui_bx + 2, ui_by + 3, 70, 36, ui_j * 32, ui_ln);
    gfx_setfont(5); colInk(0.8);
    sprintf(#ui_t, "%c  %d STEPS", 65 + ui_j, ui_ln); xstr(ui_bx + 4, ui_by + 44, #ui_t);
    (pg_curSlot == ui_j && pg_curStep >= 0) ? ( colWhite(0.9); xcirc(ui_bx + 66, ui_by + 49, 2.2, 1); );
    (inBox(ui_bx, ui_by, 74, 58) && uiClick) ? ( ui_slotSel(ui_j); );
    pg_hint(ui_bx, ui_by, 74, 58, "Slot overview: click = edit and play this slot. The number is the pattern length");
  );
  gfx_setfont(5); colInk(0.6);
  pg_strF(256, 606, 5, "PRINT THE WHOLE CHAIN: ACTION 'TT-303PATGEN PRINT SONG CHAIN' (NEEDS SEQ LINK, SEE OUTPUT)", 620, 16);
  pg_hint(256, 604, 620, 18, "How to turn the whole song chain into a MIDI item: enable SEQ LINK, select a track, run the action TT-303PATGEN Print Song Chain from the action list");
);

ui_dk && ui_tab == 3 ? (
  // ---- GALLERY: acht Kandidaten (jeder = GENERATE mit seinem Seed), Teil-Neuwuerfeln, Seed-Historie ----
  ui_gStale = (pg_galCtr == 0 || pg_galLen != ui_len) ? 1 : 0;
  ui_op(256, 452, 62, 20, "ROLL 8", "Draw eight new candidates from the current generator settings for the length of the active slot. Each candidate is exactly what GENERATE would give with its seed", 1) ? ( ui_send(70, 0, 0, 0); );
  toggle(322, 452, 60, 20, ui_gAuto, "AUTO") ? ( ui_gAuto = 1 - ui_gAuto; );
  pg_hint(322, 452, 60, 20, "AUTO: draw new candidates by itself whenever a generator setting, the slot or the length changes (this tab only)");
  ui_tgt == ui_slot ? ( ui_tgt = (ui_slot + 1) % 8; );
  sprintf(#cmb_txt, "KEEP TO %c", 65 + ui_tgt);
  ui_tgt = combo(36, 388, 452, 92, 20, ui_tgt, 8);
  pg_hint(388, 452, 92, 20, "Target slot for KEEP (click = next, arrows = -/+)");
  gfx_setfont(5); colInk(0.85); xstr(488, 457, "REROLL");
  ui_op(530, 452, 54, 20, "NOTES", "Partial reroll: a new tone sequence over the rhythm of the pattern - walk / Markov / motif, TENSION, REPEAT, OCT JUMP, RANGE and scale as in GENERATE (locked steps stay, ties follow their note)", 1) ? ( ui_send(73, 1, 0, 0); );
  ui_op(588, 452, 60, 20, "RHYTHM", "Partial reroll: a new rhythm (algorithm, DENSITY, DENS VAR, SYNCOPATION, TIES as in GENERATE); the pitch of every step stays, accents stay where the step still plays, slides are redrawn (locked steps stay)", 1) ? ( ui_send(73, 2, 0, 0); );
  ui_op(652, 452, 62, 20, "ACC+SLD", "Partial reroll: new accents (ACCENT %) and slides (SLIDE %) over the rhythm that plays now; tones and gates stay (locked steps stay)", 1) ? ( ui_send(73, 3, 0, 0); );
  ui_op(718, 452, 34, 20, "ALL", "Partial reroll: every step that is not locked comes from a new candidate", 1) ? ( ui_send(73, 4, 0, 0); );
  // Seed-Historie: ui_shi = 0 neueste
  ui_shn = min(16, PG_SH[16]);
  ui_shi = min(max(0, ui_shn - 1), max(0, ui_shi));
  ui_op(758, 452, 18, 20, "<", "Seed history: one seed further back", ui_shi < ui_shn - 1) ? ( ui_shi += 1; );
  ui_op(778, 452, 18, 20, ">", "Seed history: one seed forward", ui_shi > 0) ? ( ui_shi -= 1; );
  ui_shn > 0 ? ( ui_hseed = PG_SH[(PG_SH[16] - 1 - ui_shi) % 16]; sprintf(#ui_s, "0x%06X", ui_hseed); ) : strcpy(#ui_s, "NO SEED");
  // 1.0.4: Tooltip nennt die Generator-Generation, unter der der Eintrag entstand (aeltere Generation = Muster kann abweichen)
  ui_shn > 0 ? sprintf(#ui_t, "Seed history: GENERATE the active slot with this seed, made by generator v%d - this plug-in is v%d (SEED is set to it, LOCK stays as it is; settings as they are now)", PG_SH[17 + (PG_SH[16] - 1 - ui_shi) % 16], PG_GENVER) : strcpy(#ui_t, "Seed history: no seed used yet");
  ui_op(800, 452, 80, 20, #ui_s, #ui_t, ui_shn > 0) ? ( ui_send(75, ui_hseed, 0, 0); );
  // AUTO: Einstellungen beobachten (ohne SEED, damit TRY nicht sofort neu wuerfelt)
  ui_sig = ui_slot * 5 + ui_len * 101 + slider4 * 3 + slider5 * 7 + slider6 * 11 + slider7 * 13 + slider8 * 17 + slider9 * 19 + slider10 * 23 + slider11 * 29
         + slider12 * 31 + slider13 * 37 + slider14 * 41 + slider15 * 43 + slider16 * 47 + slider17 * 53
         + slider68 * 59;   // Review 0.9.0 F4: DENS VAR gehoert zur Signatur (Historie: endete bei slider17)
  ui_sig != ui_sigP ? ( ui_sigP = ui_sig; ui_sigT = time_precise(); ui_sigPend = 1; );
  (ui_gAuto && ui_sigPend && time_precise() - ui_sigT > 0.25) ? ( ui_sigPend = 0; ui_send(70, 0, 0, 0); );
  // Kandidaten 4 x 2
  ui_i = 0;
  loop(8,
    ui_j = ui_i;
    ui_i += 1;
    ui_cx = 256 + (ui_j & 3) * 156;
    ui_cy = 478 + (ui_j >> 2) * 76;
    panelBox(ui_cx, ui_cy, 152, 72);
    ui_gStale ? ( gfx_set(0.1, 0.1, 0.1, 1); xrect(ui_cx + 4, ui_cy + 3, 144, 34); )
              : ui_mini(ui_cx + 4, ui_cy + 3, 144, 34, PG_GAL + ui_j * 32, pg_galLen);
    gfx_setfont(5); colInk(0.7);
    ui_gStale ? strcpy(#ui_t, ui_j == 0 ? "PRESS ROLL 8" : "-") : sprintf(#ui_t, "SEED 0x%06X", PG_GS[ui_j]);
    xstr(ui_cx + 6, ui_cy + 39, #ui_t);
    ui_op(ui_cx + 4, ui_cy + 50, 68, 20, "TRY", "Put this candidate into the active slot (SEED is set to its seed; undoable). Locked steps stay", !ui_gStale) ? ( ui_send(71, ui_j, 0, 0); );
    ui_op(ui_cx + 76, ui_cy + 50, 72, 20, "KEEP", "Copy this candidate into the KEEP TO slot (undoable) without touching the active slot", !ui_gStale) ? ( ui_send(72, ui_j, ui_tgt, 0); );
  );
);

ui_dk && ui_tab == 4 ? (
  // ---- LIBRARY: die 32 Stilmuster mit Vorschau; Klick = in den aktiven Slot laden (undoable) ----
  ui_i = 0;
  loop(32,
    ui_j = ui_i;
    ui_i += 1;
    ui_cx = 256 + (ui_j & 7) * 78;
    ui_cy = 452 + (ui_j >> 3) * 44;
    ui_kh = inBox(ui_cx, ui_cy, 74, 40) ? 1 : 0;
    panelBox(ui_cx, ui_cy, 74, 40);
    ui_kh ? ( colAcid(0.8); xrrect(ui_cx, ui_cy, 74, 40, 3, 0); );
    ui_mini(ui_cx + 2, ui_cy + 2, 70, 22, M_LIB + ui_j * 16, 16);
    pg_libStr(ui_j);
    gfx_setfont(5); ui_kh ? colWhite(0.95) : colInk(0.8);
    pg_strF(ui_cx + 4, ui_cy + 26, 5, #pn, 68, 12);
    (ui_kh && uiClick) ? ( ui_send(20, ui_j, 0, 0); );
    pg_hint(ui_cx, ui_cy, 74, 40, "Library pattern: click = load into the active slot (16 steps, undoable). With ALGO = CLASSIC MUT the generator mutates these patterns");
  );
);

// P25 (Harmonisierung 2/3): Sollform der Suite. Kopfzeilen-Tooltips (Preset-Leiste je Element, OPTIONS) ueber tt_modtips() aus dem
// Kit; uikit_end() zuletzt. Historie: pg_barhints(); tt_tipflush(); pg_rflush(); uikit_end(); standen vor tt_pb_post/tth_post.
 
// Preset-Leiste (Preset-Modul) in der Kopfzeile links neben OPTIONS, Designraster (292,20), 250 breit; Aktionen laufen als Kommandos im @block
// P25 (A11): FACTORY nur mit zwei freien Ring-Plaetzen (sonst blieb pg_pbSeq != pg_pbAck fuer immer); A7: Undo-Marke anfordern.
pg_pa = tt_pb_post(OX + 292 * SC, OY + 20 * SC, SC);
// 0.6.1 (Review P-G): Preset-/Szenen-/INIT-Auftraege teilen sich PG_PBA und tt_pb_buf. Ein neuer Auftrag wird erst gestartet, wenn der
// vorige im @block bestaetigt ist (pg_pbSeq == pg_pbAck) und zwei Ring-Plaetze frei sind; bis dahin wird er gemerkt (der letzte gewinnt).
// Vorher ueberschrieb ein zweiter Auftrag bei stehendem @block (FX umgangen/offline) den Puffer des ersten.
// Historie: pg_pa direkt ausgewertet. 1.0.6 (dsh F4): SAVE (3) laeuft seitdem ueber Kommando 39 im @block und geht wie die anderen durch den Aufschub.
(pg_pa > 0) ? ( pg_pbDefPa = pg_pa; pg_pbDefArg = tt_pb_arg; pg_pa = 0; );
(pg_pbDefPa > 0 && pg_pbSeq == pg_pbAck && pg_ringFree() >= 3) ? (
  pg_pa = pg_pbDefPa; tt_pb_arg = pg_pbDefArg; pg_pbDefPa = 0;
);
pg_pa == 1 ? (
  tt_pb_arg < PG_NLIB ? (
    // 0.6.0 (F7): kein pg_set(36) mehr (LIB IDX wird nirgends gelesen, kostete einen Undo-Schritt); Historie: pg_set(36, tt_pb_arg);
    pg_ringFree() >= 2 ? ( pg_pbSeq += 1; pg_post(20, tt_pb_arg, 0, 0); pg_post(32, 0, 0, 0); pg_undoNeed = 1; );   // FACTORY: Bibliotheksmuster in den aktiven Slot (wie die fruehere LOAD-Taste)
  ) : (
    pg_pbSend(52, tt_pb_arg - PG_NLIB);   // 1.0.6 (dsh F4): Szenenbau + Anwenden im @block (vorher baute @gfx den Staging-Puffer mitten im Block-Lauf)
  );
)
: pg_pa == 2 ? ( pg_pbSend(34, tt_pb_arg); )   // 1.0.6 (dsh F4): Fetch + Apply ganz im @block (vorher las @gfx die Bank, waehrend ein Commit dort schreiben konnte)
: pg_pa == 3 ? ( pg_post(39, tt_pb_arg, 0, 0); )   // 1.0.6 (dsh F4): Capture + Commit gehoeren in den @block; keine Marke/kein Undo (SAVE aendert kein Muster)
: pg_pa == 4 ? ( pg_pbSend(31, 0); );
(pg_pbSeq != pg_pbAck) ? ( tt_pb_reset = 1; ) : tt_pb_track(pg_pbSum());   // Referenz fuer den Stern erst nach der Ausfuehrung im @block
// P25 (A7): Undo-Marke (Kommando 36) einmal je Frame HINTER die Muster-Kommandos dieses Frames; im @block ruft sie tt_undo(), tth_post
// erzeugt den Undo-Punkt "Edit FX" (sliderchange(-1)), sobald die Maustaste los ist. Ring voll -> im naechsten Frame erneut.
pg_undoNeed ? ( pg_post(36, 0, 0, 0) ? ( pg_undoNeed = 0; ); );
pg_seedNew ? ( pg_seedNew = 0; sliderchange(slider2); );   // P25 (A7): neuer Seed aus dem @block (NEW / GENERATE ohne LOCK) -> Host
// OPTIONS-Button (Theme-Modul) rechts neben der Leiste, Designraster (550,20); Box legt sich als Overlay darueber
ui_tc = tth_post(OX + 550 * SC, OY + 20 * SC, SC);
ui_tc >= 0 ? ( slider64 = ui_tc; sliderchange(slider64); slider_automate(slider64); );
tt_modtips(); tt_tipflush(); // 02.10.2026: nach allen Overlays
uikit_end();
